# Lanternlight - ignore rules
#
# Two jobs: keep build/tool noise out, and keep operator PII out. The second
# job is the one that actually matters - see the PII HAZARD block below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch / working dirs - never part of the published tree
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scratchpad/
_scratch/
scratch/
tmp/
.tmp/
ops/runtime/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Captures, frames and screenshots
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
frames/
captures/
capture/
screenshots/
frames/**
captures/**
capture/**
screenshots/**
frames/*.png
captures/*.png
capture/*.png
screenshots/*.png
frames/*.jpg
captures/*.jpg
capture/*.jpg
screenshots/*.jpg
frames/*.jpeg
captures/*.jpeg
frames/*.webp
captures/*.webp
frames/*.mp4
captures/*.mp4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
logs/**
*.log
*.log.[0-9]
*.log.[0-9][0-9]
*.logs

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Game saves and extracted / derived game data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sav
*.sav.bak
*.savegame
data/mhdata/
data/mhdata/**
data/extracted/
data/raw/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
API-Key-*.txt
*api-key*.txt
*apikey*.txt
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
.env
.env.*
secrets.json
credentials.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent / editor / OS local config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .claude/ is DELIBERATELY TRACKED here, unlike in the sibling projects on this
# machine. The governance in it - the session default, the subagent definitions,
# the ASCII and commit gates - is the point of the repo being reproducible. A
# fresh clone that gets CLAUDE.md but not the hooks and agents gets half the
# rules and none of the enforcement. Only genuinely machine-local files are
# excluded below.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/**/local.*
.claude/projects/
.claude/todos/
.claude/statsig/
.claude/shell-snapshots/
.mcp.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ===========================================================================
# PII HAZARD - anything copied out of the game's Saved tree
# ===========================================================================
#
# Mistfall Hunter writes a log and save tree under the local application data
# directory (on Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\MistfallHunter\Saved\). Those files are
# NOT anonymous. Observed contents include, at minimum:
#
#   - the player's SteamID64
#   - the player's Steam persona name
#   - GSDK openID / userId values
#   - an Epic Online Services ProductUserId
#   - geolocation resolved from the player's public IP address
#
# Any of those, committed once, is public forever - a force-push does not
# unpublish a value someone already cloned or that a mirror already indexed.
#
# RULE: never copy anything out of that tree into the repo working directory.
# If you must inspect a real log, read it in place, outside the repo. If a
# sample is genuinely needed for a test, hand-author a synthetic fixture with
# obviously fake identifiers - do not redact a real one, because redaction is
# a per-field allowlist problem and the next game patch adds a field.
#
# The patterns below are a backstop for when that rule is broken anyway. The
# pre-commit hook in .githooks/ is a second backstop. Neither is the primary
# control; the primary control is not copying the files.
# ===========================================================================
MistfallHunter/
**/MistfallHunter/Saved/
**/Saved/Logs/
**/Saved/SaveGames/
**/Saved/Crashes/
Saved/
*MistfallHunter*.log
*MistfallHunter*.sav
mistfall_saved/
game_logs/
game_saves/
pii/
private/
